@ngdoc error
@name $sanitize:uinput
@fullName Failed to sanitize html because the input is unstable
@description

This error occurs when the `$sanitize` sanitizer checks the sanitized html for a possible mXSS payload and the check
fails, because the browser keeps changing the html each time it parses it. This could be a sign that the input contains
code exploiting an mXSS vulnerability in the browser.

mXSS attacks exploit browser bugs that cause some browsers to parse certain html strings into DOM, which once serialized
doesn't match the original input. These browser bugs can be exploited by attackers to create a payload which looks
harmless to sanitizers, but due to mutations caused by the browser is turned into dangerous code once processed after
sanitization.
